[{:db/id "q-94807/selection/c6b1a09baa2f74bafe6ffbd397096c9ba5a48e0f32c8e2418c188e29ca93f326" :answer/id #uuid "6a1eb1df-2deb-5d1e-ad76-5ace4dce98f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of matrices is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807/selection/7678b385dd3cb999bde413618dfea159a1430df4309b864bcd9bdabd9f06fe19" :answer/id #uuid "31989510-9ee3-533e-ba1e-dbaada39a136" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807/selection/7531b5a9c07890e6233a3a0929ee26d2bdef4f2ab17cfbd63cb5fb15d88dae22" :answer/id #uuid "531c2d53-e212-5909-8ba9-484863df4a59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot A\\ne A$ for all $A\\in K$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807/selection/908e72bd8ff5d6c572d8a6fde3d52b81f12c76405327939401017d778d5f8f9b" :answer/id #uuid "e822e1fc-9467-5db2-b2b9-2e54f6438e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of matrices is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807/selection/743dc49b8159bd36a703426d40f16d9fd0b780d9bd24234d08481fb6157dc4d8" :answer/id #uuid "33bc630d-d0c0-5066-b1ce-17330dcdabf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of matrices do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec4fdc0-c432-52d0-af9b-88539b8e2fc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94807/selection/7678b385dd3cb999bde413618dfea159a1430df4309b864bcd9bdabd9f06fe19" :answer-field/choices ["q-94807/selection/c6b1a09baa2f74bafe6ffbd397096c9ba5a48e0f32c8e2418c188e29ca93f326" "q-94807/selection/7678b385dd3cb999bde413618dfea159a1430df4309b864bcd9bdabd9f06fe19" "q-94807/selection/7531b5a9c07890e6233a3a0929ee26d2bdef4f2ab17cfbd63cb5fb15d88dae22" "q-94807/selection/908e72bd8ff5d6c572d8a6fde3d52b81f12c76405327939401017d778d5f8f9b" "q-94807/selection/743dc49b8159bd36a703426d40f16d9fd0b780d9bd24234d08481fb6157dc4d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94807" :question/id #uuid "4e9325bc-24c1-5d82-b1cc-1e1fb76a771a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94807" :question/problem "Let $K$ be the set of all $2\\times 1$ matrices $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],$ such that $x,y\\in R$ and $x+y=1.$  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$** *  \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94807/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94807"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection/40ad095557e08ef1ff85bd119d4dde784b6fb08c0ea46bbacc50857d6cf704e1" :answer/id #uuid "93950d71-49ab-5d0d-979c-95c7a0e6b532" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Y$ does not contain the zero element" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection/977f837af8c0198d062be3cc31bfe2ed1d69f48687cc8ebfa63a7bf6acfc6f3d" :answer/id #uuid "171a1a9b-b707-5744-b4d1-6b9dfc2d920f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection/39396d1deaad7a3a960e85d22612bb7bb543de3ecce4cc7b581353775929047c" :answer/id #uuid "aea792ce-4a6e-5721-9a18-f99292949277" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection/6ad2b2228f22bb040074ddbe81f1ad1258ede7e36d91b1761eb676697c80a164" :answer/id #uuid "c6f8dea0-a011-58db-a415-7ee98ad9d04d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$  do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection/3ef8dd95aeb46b1f07e813f30759118288e31d346ee0a03f4d0932bdff343803" :answer/id #uuid "dc50024b-9085-5119-8f2d-a8ca14bd95e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c74e80-66a0-5e58-b9e1-e1d5d2a42b4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94808/selection/3ef8dd95aeb46b1f07e813f30759118288e31d346ee0a03f4d0932bdff343803" :answer-field/choices ["q-94808/selection/40ad095557e08ef1ff85bd119d4dde784b6fb08c0ea46bbacc50857d6cf704e1" "q-94808/selection/977f837af8c0198d062be3cc31bfe2ed1d69f48687cc8ebfa63a7bf6acfc6f3d" "q-94808/selection/39396d1deaad7a3a960e85d22612bb7bb543de3ecce4cc7b581353775929047c" "q-94808/selection/6ad2b2228f22bb040074ddbe81f1ad1258ede7e36d91b1761eb676697c80a164" "q-94808/selection/3ef8dd95aeb46b1f07e813f30759118288e31d346ee0a03f4d0932bdff343803"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94808" :question/id #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" :question/math-academy-id "q-94808" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94808/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94808"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection/05fae4cd46a191738d0d3c6f2a345fe9fa2e212bfdaf40a32b899265e5dde17a" :answer/id #uuid "0ab86367-0fa9-543e-b61f-a4044ead541b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{A1},\\text{A3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection/beded7960e17db7da03c8e3c457aeaf94f4821e8fe20146c08303d98d38c26cb" :answer/id #uuid "29baacef-5efd-5a4e-b22e-75802a5059d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{A3},\\text{A4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection/9773c1b89ad2083ed3e943b907af5ee05c634005d8044b6ba89b9d0eddeb7e88" :answer/id #uuid "2f464c7c-4e06-5def-b447-30f0dae4c1b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{A2},\\text{A4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection/3ed650075c96cd0031cec833401f8b2ed01a30240a3e19248092492ea2f5b450" :answer/id #uuid "383e3bf7-4541-5eee-876e-909810f624cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{A2},\\text{A3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection/016970670debfe62620ee914c30b9634922c1d1d1f94bfd4e1491ed9180cdc68" :answer/id #uuid "92c687cc-45a6-5292-9a6d-4211b654eb72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{A1},\\text{A4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a501bedf-1c70-5820-92cf-3a7a11f55678" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94937/selection/016970670debfe62620ee914c30b9634922c1d1d1f94bfd4e1491ed9180cdc68" :answer-field/choices ["q-94937/selection/05fae4cd46a191738d0d3c6f2a345fe9fa2e212bfdaf40a32b899265e5dde17a" "q-94937/selection/beded7960e17db7da03c8e3c457aeaf94f4821e8fe20146c08303d98d38c26cb" "q-94937/selection/9773c1b89ad2083ed3e943b907af5ee05c634005d8044b6ba89b9d0eddeb7e88" "q-94937/selection/3ed650075c96cd0031cec833401f8b2ed01a30240a3e19248092492ea2f5b450" "q-94937/selection/016970670debfe62620ee914c30b9634922c1d1d1f94bfd4e1491ed9180cdc68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94937" :question/id #uuid "f54d0d72-c3d0-5096-886c-e29b889e3841" :question/math-academy-id "q-94937" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A1\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A4\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94937/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00" :answer/id #uuid "a664ff91-48f1-5ae4-ada4-3fa4b166eb07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection/eb57353034a62a867325ffbf5c3603e09d85e72840a34606df91d959ee49bb75" :answer/id #uuid "02790ff3-06cd-5da0-9e4b-98da0a0d0833" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection/c26bc0b99b0b461cbb162012172b782569b27c43d4a833b5412a2affe482fe80" :answer/id #uuid "22a4e1ec-05fc-513a-bbbb-196e2f363402" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not commutative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection/af0eba804fe4e1984fdee36b872595a6820b8598cca0173b2959526c5870f5f7" :answer/id #uuid "07f60e7f-6e02-5f1c-b720-366aa10a0075" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not associative" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection/39ce4feac3754f14f312ebbf40b6b6942599ab62d9f7528045b3064023739dd6" :answer/id #uuid "08f26cd7-b4e2-533f-9258-7e760fd6f507" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in L$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1be1f1ff-185c-5903-841f-0172a0c5e527" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106930/selection/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00" :answer-field/choices ["q-106930/selection/83f490698e6e183c9c2b74efe3d16ee9060e1e0d6cfa7bd24f10d24f6c178e00" "q-106930/selection/eb57353034a62a867325ffbf5c3603e09d85e72840a34606df91d959ee49bb75" "q-106930/selection/c26bc0b99b0b461cbb162012172b782569b27c43d4a833b5412a2affe482fe80" "q-106930/selection/af0eba804fe4e1984fdee36b872595a6820b8598cca0173b2959526c5870f5f7" "q-106930/selection/39ce4feac3754f14f312ebbf40b6b6942599ab62d9f7528045b3064023739dd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106930" :question/id #uuid "15beea94-47dc-575a-be81-e2d3b2547e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106930" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=ax+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)=x+1,$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2x+2.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin L$ because the constant term is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in L.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of real valued functions satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection/2df53d7033d468a797adc4e4a7e243c9e98f6c84849b9c640422aa67819abd59" :answer/id #uuid "cf08fb6b-e3b2-5444-b00f-2d86b3d4ef55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection/e18a8c978383357532770f06b84acc89aa5f3128d451f9b0945a10b52440b3ce" :answer/id #uuid "ae72d013-20aa-5576-9391-4efcb759de85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection/5fb9cbe19bce8b9f1906633b1d301c029bda6936056b92d8edbca1739aa51ba5" :answer/id #uuid "15d8720c-d1e6-54d7-95d2-a4a228ee7476" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection/31d38c50d8c71e2d42a7662c1b2cc6f833dac5bd7622055ae5233a91fa2d814c" :answer/id #uuid "85ad6021-1111-585d-ba15-9f99f5bc0e48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection/2c2447ab340bd334a7ec280542f9cc734633c51efddc05f97d168842833c9695" :answer/id #uuid "3638f7b7-802a-5b50-aa15-d0eaadee0ff1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e95976d-6212-5c03-ba82-7f260ee5e5e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106940/selection/5fb9cbe19bce8b9f1906633b1d301c029bda6936056b92d8edbca1739aa51ba5" :answer-field/choices ["q-106940/selection/2df53d7033d468a797adc4e4a7e243c9e98f6c84849b9c640422aa67819abd59" "q-106940/selection/e18a8c978383357532770f06b84acc89aa5f3128d451f9b0945a10b52440b3ce" "q-106940/selection/5fb9cbe19bce8b9f1906633b1d301c029bda6936056b92d8edbca1739aa51ba5" "q-106940/selection/31d38c50d8c71e2d42a7662c1b2cc6f833dac5bd7622055ae5233a91fa2d814c" "q-106940/selection/2c2447ab340bd334a7ec280542f9cc734633c51efddc05f97d168842833c9695"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106940" :question/id #uuid "01cc4fec-23d5-5237-aea5-3e56464042be" :question/math-academy-id "q-106940" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $y$ and $z$ are vectors such that $x+y=z+x$ for some $x\\in V$, then $y=z.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =z+x &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(z+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =z+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =z+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =z &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-106940/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106940"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
